title: Authorizations › New Case › Reopen and resume a case
route: /authorizations/new/:draftId
intro: What happens when the address names a case: it reopens where it was left, a case that was already sent says so, a case at another site is not available to a viewer who cannot see that site, and an unknown id says so. A case whose agents already ran never reopens on Intake; one saved while the agents worked (the old step 4) opens Clinical documentation scrolled to Authorization preparation.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "A case id is in the address"
start s2 "Click a button on a draft row in Authorizations (In progress)\n'Continue', 'Watch', 'Answer' or 'Review and sign'"
start s3 "Click 'Open in review and sign' or 'Send to payer' on a case page\nA draft is made from the request, or the one it has is brought up to date"
process pReq "Draft opens on Review & submit when the request is ready\non Clinical documentation at Authorization preparation when agents still have work\nNever a blank draft"
decision d3 "Is there a case with that id?"
screen sc1 "New Case\n'We could not find that draft'\n'It may have been cleared when the demo data was reset.'"
click c1 "Click 'Start a new case'"
goto gNew "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › How a case starts and resumes"
decision dSite "Is the case at a site in view?"
screen scOut "'This case is not available at Site B'\n'R-0975 belongs to Site B. Dr. Rivera can see Site A only.'\nNo patient, payer or dates are shown"
click cShow "Click 'Show Site B'\nOnly for a viewer who may see both sites"
process pShow "The site view switches to Site B\nThe case opens"
decision d4 "Was it signed and sent?"
screen sc2 "'R-1234 was sent'\n'Signed and sent (demo)', or 'Already with the payer'"
click c2 "Click 'Open the case', or 'Open it on the Dashboard'"
click c3 "Click 'Back to Authorizations'"
decision d5 "Did the agents already run, with the case still on an earlier step?"
process p9 "Opens on Clinical documentation, scrolled to Authorization preparation, when fewer than ten agents are done\nelse on Review & submit\nA later click in the stepper is not undone"
screen sc3 "New Case\nLink 'Authorizations', the header card 'New Case' with the case id and the 'Authorization type' dropdown\nThe stepper with each step's state, the workflow line, then the step"
click c4 "Click the link 'Authorizations'"
decision d6 "Which step is the case on?"
process pNarrow "Narrowing the site view while a blank case is open\nA case with no patient and no ID moves to the site in view; one with an ID or a patient stays at its own site"
goto gCm "Continues in: Authorizations › Worklist › Arrive and read the views"
goto gDash "Continues in: Dashboard\nOpens the request"
goto gCase "Continues in: Authorizations › Case page › Send to payer and review and sign"
goto gSites "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Sites and scope"
goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Intake › Initial authorization"
goto g1b "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Intake › Find a patient and the authorization"
goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Eligibility & Benefits › Initial authorization"
goto g3 "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Clinical documentation › The checklist and Continue"
goto g4 "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Authorization preparation › Start the run and watch it"
goto g5 "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Review & submit › The draft and the summary"

s3 --> pReq --> d3
s1 --> d3
s2 --> d3
d3 -->|No| sc1 --> c1 --> gNew
d3 -->|Yes| dSite
dSite -->|No| scOut
scOut --> cShow --> pShow --> d4
scOut -.-> gSites
dSite -->|Yes| d4
d4 -->|Yes| sc2
sc2 --> c2 --> gDash
sc2 --> c3 --> gCm
d4 -->|No| d5
d5 -->|Yes| p9 --> sc3
d5 -->|No| sc3
sc3 --> c4 --> gCm
sc3 --> d6
sc3 -.-> pNarrow
s3 -.-> gCase
d6 -->|Intake, initial or retroactive| g1
d6 -->|Intake, review, renewal or modification| g1b
d6 -->|Eligibility & Benefits| g2
d6 -->|Clinical documentation| g3
d6 -->|Clinical documentation, agents started| g4
d6 -->|Review & submit| g5
